        "Phase 2 startup correction (namespace error)."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    skos:definition "Phase 2 startup found that v1.0.1 review used wrong namespace (quality-criteria# instead of quality#); 5 of 6 claimed gaps were partially or fully closed already. This is BP-2 (read raw files) at the audit layer, not just the artifact layer."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-05-15T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy oe-prov:Activity_OEPackRelease_v17_33_0 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso kb:OEPACK_BP2_C1Inventory .

kb:Refinement_PostSupersessionAuditReporting a kb:Refinement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Refinement: Post-Supersession Audit Reporting"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "Migrated from rev:Refinement_PostSupersessionAuditReporting (catalogue v1.1.0 canonical). (See pre-migration source statement(s) above.)"@en,
        "Refinement_PostSupersessionAuditReporting_v1_0_7_13 — emerged from FIX work-package empirical re-verification, 2026-05-13. Retained in v1.1.0 consolidation as governance vocabulary."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    skos:definition """Audit-time mismatch counts MUST be reported in two
buckets:
  (a) raw count of mismatches in the corpus filesystem;
  (b) count of mismatches that survive after SUPERSESSION_MAP is applied
      (the post-supersession canonical set).

Only (b) requires corrective action; (a) reflects historical artifact
retention. AUDIT documents that report only (a) overstate severity. The
empirical case: AUDIT 2026-05-13 reported 15 BP-D7 mismatches; FIX
empirical re-verification on canonical post-supersession files found
only 1 actually still needed correction."""@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso kb:BestPractice_D7_StrictBP3VersionSemantics .

kb:Refinement_StrandedClassPolicy a kb:Refinement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Refinement: Stranded-Class Policy (decision rubric)"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "Migrated from rev:Refinement_StrandedClassPolicy (catalogue v1.1.0 canonical). (See pre-migration source statement(s) above.)"@en,
        "Phase 2.9 stranded-class triage outcome (24 classes reviewed). Origin: v1.0.6.1 PATCH. Retained in v1.1.0 consolidation as governance vocabulary."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    skos:definition """A formal decision rubric for handling classes that
have no parent in the local namespace and no obvious parent in upstream
(prov, skos, dc, foaf, etc.).

Decision rubric (in order):
  (a) Add a prov-based or skos-based parent when the class has natural-fit
      semantics: entity-typed → prov:Entity; concept-typed → skos:Concept;
      plan-typed → prov:Plan; bundle-typed → prov:Bundle.
  (b) Declare intentional top-level via release_preflight TOP_LEVEL_OK when
      the class is itself an umbrella concept with no natural parent (root
      of a discipline subtree).
  (c) Mark the class as 'orphan-pending-review' if no natural-fit parent
      exists AND the class is not an umbrella. These accumulate in a
      review queue tracked in the catalogue."""@en .

kb:Refinement_SubjectBridgePattern a kb:Refinement,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Refinement: Subject + Bridge Pattern (architectural)"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "Migrated from rev:Refinement_SubjectBridgePattern (catalogue v1.1.0 canonical). (See pre-migration source statement(s) above.)"@en,
        "Refinement_SubjectBridgePattern_v1_0_7_11 — emerged from v17.18.0 AE-Performance separation analysis (PRFO authoring discussion). Retained in v1.1.0 consolidation as governance vocabulary."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    skos:definition """The OE ecosystem uses a SUBJECT + BRIDGE pattern for
handling cross-cutting concerns:

SUBJECT ontologies hold concepts for a single coherent domain.
  Examples: OQC (ontology quality), a reliability ontology (reliability engineering),
            AMOD (asset management), AE (algorithm efficiency).
  Properties: self-contained as far as possible; reusable outside
              the OE ecosystem; one cohesive subject per file (per
              BP-D18 in-place evolution rule).

BRIDGE ontologies hold the inter-domain relationships that connect
two or more SUBJECT ontologies without diluting either's cohesion.
  Examples: ae_bridge (connects AE to OQC/a reliability ontology via justifiedByComplexity
            and measurementOf relations), oem_bridge.
  Properties: properties-only or very small class set; declares foreign
              imports; intentionally narrow scope.

The pattern preserves cohesion (BP-D18 ruling) while expressing genuine
cross-domain semantic connections."""@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso kb:BestPractice_D18_LangTagOnXsdStringInconsistency .

