kb:Roadmap_DTUse100Rate a kb:RoadmapPlan,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Roadmap: 100% DT-Use rate (every declared DT property used in ABox)"@en ;
    kb:hasCurrentValue 0.55 ;
    kb:hasSteps """Current state per v17.30.0 measurement:
  - ontology-engineering: 100% (target met)
  - measurement: 75%
  - reliability: 67%
  - ae: 60%
  - oepack-release-history: 60%
  - quality: 29%
  - configuration: 23%
  - risk: 20%
  - core, meta, sto, performance: no DT props in NS (n/a per L-47)

STEP 1 (v17.32.0): For each DT property unused in ABox, locate the home class via rdfs:domain (post-v17.27.0 most have domain). Author at least one representative instance with that property populated. Per L-49: each instance must be plausibly real (not synthetic placeholder).

STEP 2 (v17.33.0): Convert IKÜ course example data into ABox individuals — natural source of real-world content for amod/risk/quality. Per the method author prior: 22+ IKÜ course games exist as test cases for GPPT.

STEP 3 (v17.34.0): For genuinely-unused DT properties (no real-world usage), consider DEPRECATION via owl:deprecated rather than synthetic instance creation. This is the L-40 anti-gaming alternative — better to retire vocabulary than fabricate ABox.

Per L-40 disclosure: 100% DT-Use is NOT always desirable. Some DT properties are appropriately rare (apply to edge cases). Target should be "every DT prop EITHER has ≥1 instance OR is deprecated with rationale" — same metric, honest framing."""^^xsd:string ;
    kb:hasTargetValue 1.000 ;
    kb:targetsMetric "dt_property_use_rate"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "OE Pack v17.31.0 item #4 — codified plan to reach 100% DT-Use. Plan is queryable."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-05-15T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy oe-prov:Activity_OEPackRelease_v17_31_0 .

kb:Roadmap_SHACL100Coverage a kb:RoadmapPlan,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Roadmap: 100% SHACL NodeShape coverage on example.org classes"@en ;
    kb:hasCurrentValue 0.064 ;
    kb:hasSteps """STEP 1 (v17.32.0): Generate auto-skeleton NodeShapes for every owl:Class — one-line shape with sh:targetClass only. Brings coverage to 100% mechanically but with no semantic content (placeholder for richer constraints).

STEP 2 (v17.33.x): For each subject, author meaningful property constraints — sh:minCount, sh:datatype, sh:in for enumerations, sh:pattern for IRI-shape conventions. Priority order by subject DT-Use rate (highest first):
  - ontology-engineering (100% DT-Use): trivial; mostly done
  - oe-measurement (75%): codify ThresholdRow property constraints
  - reliability (67%): codify FailureMode, RiskMitigation constraints
  - algorithm-efficiency (60%): codify EfficiencyClass, RecurrenceRelation
  - oepack-release-history (60%): release-record constraints
  - quality, amod, risk (20-29%): scaffold-only; awaits content authoring

STEP 3 (v17.34.0): Add Regression_AllClassesHaveShape to catch any new class lacking a shape.

Per L-40 honest disclosure: STEP 1 is mechanical, achieves coverage metric but does NOT improve validation quality. STEP 2 is where real value comes. Plan should not be reported as "100% coverage" after only STEP 1."""^^xsd:string ;
    kb:hasTargetValue 1.000 ;
    kb:targetsMetric "shacl_nodeshape_coverage"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "OE Pack v17.31.0 item #2 — codified plan to reach 100% SHACL coverage. Plan is queryable: `SELECT ?step WHERE { :Roadmap_SHACL100Coverage kb:hasSteps ?step }`."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-05-15T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy oe-prov:Activity_OEPackRelease_v17_31_0 .

