kb:Lesson_L_40_ObservationsVsDecisionsInDisclosures a kb:LessonsLearned,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "L-40: Distinguish Observations From Decisions In Disclosures"@en ;
    kb:hasLessonId "L-40"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "Surfaced at step 10b (OE v1.2.0 + OEM v1.2.0 deferred-class absorption). The DevelopmentProcess subtree size (155 classes) was an observation I had already resolved by anchoring under kb:OntologyEngineeringDiscipline. I framed it as a deferred ruling unnecessarily. User correction made the discipline pattern explicit."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    skos:definition "When writing 'what surprised me' / disclosures in work-package READMEs, distinguish observations from decisions. An item the implementer already resolved with a disposition is an OBSERVATION — note it as a fact, do not invite further user input. A genuine fork in the road where the implementer cannot pick without user input is a DECISION — mark it clearly as 'ruling needed' so it gets visibility. Mixing the two inflates the user's decision burden and dilutes the surfacing of real questions. Surfaced at step 10b when the user explicitly asked 'what really are you waiting for?' after I framed an observation as a deferred ruling."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-05-15T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy oe-prov:Activity_OEPackRelease_v17_33_0 .

<http://example.org/oe-method/backlog#Objective_CompleteEcosystem> a bl:Objective,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Deploy the whole ecosystem; remove only personal usages, data and packages"@en ;
    bl:contributesToGoal <http://example.org/oe-method/backlog#Goal_MethodTransfers> ;
    bl:hasBaselineValue 0.0 ;
    bl:hasSuccessMetric "governed TBox classes carrying at least one individual, as a percentage" ;
    bl:hasTargetDirection <http://example.org/oe-method/backlog#Dir_Increase> ;
    bl:hasTargetValue 100.0 ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/oe-method/backlog> ;
    skos:definition """Removal is scoped to four categories and nothing else: personal identity,
institutional identity, business data, and other parties' packages. Every operational artifact
carries over. Measured baseline: 147 files in the governing pack, of which 79 are removals in
those four categories and 68 carry over."""@en .

