kb:BestPractice_D2_NeverTrustSummaries a kb:BestPractice,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Never trust summaries — read raw files"@en ;
    kb:hasBestPracticeId "BP-D2"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "Migrated from rev:BestPractice_D2_NeverTrustSummaries (catalogue PATCH chain v1.0.5..v1.0.7.13). (See pre-migration source statement(s) above.)"@en,
        "User instruction restated across multiple turns: 'Never trust to the summaries or deflated content.'"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    skos:definition """Closure documents, README files, and conversational summaries describe what their authors INTENDED to ship. The actual artifact may differ. Always read the raw TTL/MD/code file with the view or bash tool before making claims about its content. Specifically:

  1. SHA-256 verify against MANIFEST_SHA256.txt before reading.
  2. Open the actual file (view or cat), not a summary.
  3. For ontologies: parse with rdflib, count triples, query for the specific axioms claimed.
  4. For closure documents claiming 'V=0 W=0' or 'HermiT CONSISTENT': independently re-run the validators on the actual data graph.
  5. For SHA-256 claims: re-compute and compare.

Verified value: across this study, 'never trust summaries' caught 3 distinct defects (D-PHASE2-1, D-PHASE2-2, D-PHASE3-1) that closure-document summaries explicitly claimed were CONSISTENT/CONFORMANT."""@en ;
    skos:related <http://example.org/oe-ecosystem-review#LessonLearned_31_PropertyDomainSemantics> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-05-15T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy oe-prov:Activity_OEPackRelease_v17_33_0 .

kb:Lesson_L_95_GateMustBeProvenDiscriminating a kb:LessonsLearned,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "L-95: a governance/verification gate must be proven discriminating (positive PASS + negative FAIL fixture)"@en ;
    kb:hasLessonId "L-95"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "Adopted from STG registrant governed lesson SL-01 (stg_lessons_abox_v1_6_0.ttl, stg:proposedToOEE true), ORCP Phase D, OE Pack v20.23.15. Screened against OEE 99 lessons + 56 BPs by reading full definitions (not keyword match); confirmed genuinely additive (no existing OEE lesson states this). STG is an external peer governance ecosystem; lesson generalized from its gate-engineering domain."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <http://stg.org/governance#SL_01> ;
    skos:definition "A gate that declares a method but is never shown to FAIL a known-bad input verifies nothing. Every gate must be paired with a positive fixture it passes AND a mutated negative fixture it fails; an unfallible gate is decorative. Companion to L-90 (validate the governing suite) and BP-X1 (disclose config): those govern WHICH suite and HOW; this governs whether the gate can fail at all."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-06-24T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor ;
    rdfs:seeAlso kb:BestPractice_BP_X1_ConformanceClaimDisclosureDiscipline,
        kb:Lesson_L_90_ValidateTheSuiteThatGovernsTheArtifact .

<http://example.org/oe-method/backlog> dcterms:identifier "oe-method-backlog" ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/oemethod-governance> ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-06T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:comment """Backlog and roadmap for the full OE ecosystem deployment as a generic
distributable. Expressed in the Backlog & Roadmap Semantic Framework vocabulary rather than as an
ad-hoc plan document, so the work is queryable, gate-checkable, and refinable by the same rules
that govern every other package here.

Supersedes the ad-hoc plan: that plan's keep-list was a filename glob, which silently excluded
every populated ABox and produced a package of unpopulated classes — the failure L-71 names."""@en,
        "Module membership added for the package consolidation (BP-D54): every named subject says dcterms:isPartOf its module. No other change."@en ;
    owl:imports <http://example.org/backlog> ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/oe-method/backlog/1.0.0> ;
    owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/oe-method/backlog/1.0.1> ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.1" .

<http://example.org/knowledge-base> ns1:integratesInto <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-05-16T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:creator oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor,
        "the method author"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "ontology-engineering" ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/oemethod-governance> ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-12T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dcterms:publisher oe-prov:Org_IKU_Department_of_ComputerEngineering ;
    dcterms:rights "Copyright (c) 2025-2026 a university & the method author. Licensed under CC BY 4.0."@en ;
    dcterms:rightsHolder oe-prov:Org_IKU_Department_of_ComputerEngineering ;
    rdfs:comment "ABox v1.21.1 (PATCH) per v17.34.0 Option H — added 306 PROV-O triples (prov:wasGeneratedBy, prov:wasAttributedTo, prov:generatedAtTime) to critical ABox individuals (LessonLearned/Lesson/BestPractice/RegressionTest/RoadmapPlan/PerformanceTest/isAuthoredFromReleaseHistory-true)."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.19.0 (MINOR) per v17.31.0 — added 10 RegressionTest individuals + 2 RoadmapPlan individuals (item #2 SHACL 100%; item #4 DT-Use 100%)."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.19.1 (PATCH) per v17.31.0 — corrected Regression_LessonsCountAtLeast50 SPARQL to UNION over both LessonLearned + Lesson classes per L-18. Regression suite caught this classification gap on first run (L-40 evidence the suite works as designed)."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.19.2 (PATCH) per v17.31.0 — added L-52 + BP-D26. Lessons: 51 → 52 (47 LessonLearned + 6 Lesson). BPs: 33 → 34."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.20.0 (MINOR) per v17.32.0 — added BP-D27 + Regression_AllClassesHaveShape. BPs: 34 → 35; RegressionTests: 10 → 11."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.21.0 (MINOR) per v17.33.0 — added L-53 + BP-D28. Lessons: 52 → 53; BPs: 35 → 36."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.22.0 (MINOR) per v17.34.0 — added L-54 + BP-D29 + Regression_CriticalABoxHasPROV. Lessons: 53 → 54; BPs: 36 → 37; RegressionTests: 11 → 12."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.23.0 (MINOR) per v17.35.0 — added L-55 + BP-D30 + Regression_OEMeasurement_NoSkeletonShapes. Lessons: 54→55; BPs: 37→38; RegressionTests: 12→13."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.24.0 per v17.36.0 — added Regression_Reliability_NoSkeletonShapes."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.30.0 (MINOR) per v17.42.0 — added L-56, Regression_OntologyEngineering_NoSkeletonShapes, Regression_Ecosystem_NoSkeletonShapes. Lessons: 55→56; RegressionTests: 23→25 (added 2 in this release)."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.31.0 (MINOR) per v17.43.0 — added L-57 + Regression_DeferToGPropertiesAreDeprecated. Lessons: 56 → 57; RegressionTests: 25 → 26."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.32.0 (MINOR) per v17.44.0 — integrated 5 BestPractices (BP-D31..D35) and 3 LessonsLearned (L-58, L-59, L-60) from a parallel course-pipeline development session. Renumbered proposed L-57..L-59 to L-58..L-60 to avoid collision with v17.43.0 L-57. Lessons: 52 → 55 (LessonLearned subclass); BPs: 38 → 43; RegressionTests: 26 (unchanged)."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.32.1 (PATCH) per v17.44.0 — fixed 8 stale rdfs:seeAlso references in v17.44.0-added individuals (BP-D31..D35 + L-58..L-60). Stale IRIs replaced with actual catalogue individual names per L-46 (full-IRI inspection discipline). BP-D5_GateWithBothImportsMergedAndStandalone → BP-D5_ValidateWithImportsMerged; BP-D24_LicenseAndPROVAtOntologyLevel → BP-D24_OntologyLevelLicenseAndProvenance; L-40_HonestDisclosures → L-40_ObservationsVsDecisionsInDisclosures."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.33.0 (MINOR) per v17.45.0 — codified upload-hygiene and response-economy disciplines: +5 BPs (D36..D40), +3 Lessons (L-61..L-63), +1 regression (BPsHaveSourceProvenance). BPs: 43 → 48; LessonLearned: 54 → 57; RegressionTests: 26 → 27. Risk analysis preceded build; preventive actions PA-1..PA-10 applied. Scope-constrained per user directive 2026-05-17."@en,
        "OE catalogue ABox v1.34.0 (MINOR) per v18.0.0 — added L-64 ScopeBleedViaSourceAttributionNarratives codifying the scope-creep failure pattern that necessitated v18.0.0. Plus 15 literal narrative rewrites cleaning WPC/Cap/RRWPC/c5 references from v17.44.0-authored individual skos:definition / dcterms:source / rdfs:comment fields."@en,
        "OE catalogue v1.15.0 (MINOR) per v17.26.0 — added L-47 (AttrR=0 dual nature) and BP-D23 (infer domain from usage). Lessons 46→47, BPs 22→23. Additive content."@en,
        "OE catalogue v1.15.1 (PATCH) per v17.26.0 — added L-48 (rdfs:domain + disjointness clash) discovered during N execution itself. Lessons 47→48."@en,
        "OE catalogue v1.16.0 (MINOR) per v17.27.0 Challenges 1+2 — added L-49 (design-intent extraction is not fabrication), L-50 (cross-branch usage blocks single rdfs:domain). Lessons 48 → 50."@en,
        "OE catalogue v1.17.0 (MINOR) per v17.28.0 — added BP-D24 (ontology-level license + PROV-O lineage requirement for industrial use). Lessons stable at 50. BPs 23 → 24 (D-numbered scheme), 31 → 32 (total)."@en,
        "OE catalogue v1.17.1 (PATCH) per v17.29.0 — added L-51 (pyshacl sh:severity must be shape-level, not sh:sparql-bnode-level). Lessons: 50 → 51."@en,
        "OE catalogue v1.18.0 (MINOR) per v17.30.0 — added BP-D25 (CQ classification discipline). Lessons stable at 51; BPs 32 → 33 (24 D-numbered + 8 OEPACK)."@en,
        "OE v1.4.1 (PATCH from v1.4.0): added two new catalogue individuals — L-45 DiagrammaticDeclarationFalsehood (LessonLearned) and BP-D20 VerifyDiagramContainmentMatchesTBox (BestPractice) — capturing the discipline for raw-verifying diagram containment claims against source-of-truth structure. Originated 2026-05-14 from the F1-redirect diagram-truth audit session. Per user decisions: name \"DiagrammaticDeclarationFalsehood\" chosen, scope GENERALIZED to any structured diagram with containment as visual primitive, BP-D20 explicitly requested as positive-discipline counterpart. No class declarations changed; pure additive PATCH."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.17.0 (MINOR) per OE Pack v20.24.0 — added L-110 (no new governance structure on a single producer's evidence; enrich the governing term and defer). Lessons: 113 -> 114. Best Practices unchanged at 59. L-109 deliberately unused (declined candidate, v20.23.36)."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.18.0 (MINOR) per OE Pack v20.25.0 - added L-111 (documentation-coverage drift is invisible to every structural gate; gate coverage in the artifact-to-prose direction). Lessons: 114 -> 115. Best Practices unchanged at 59."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.19.0 (MINOR) per OE Pack v20.26.0 - added L-112 (a mechanical repoint must exclude historical records by file class). Lessons: 115 -> 116. Best Practices unchanged at 59."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.19.1 (PATCH) per OE Pack v20.26.1 - amended L-112's classification clause from two-way to three-way (current-state / historical / generated), after a registrant implementation exposed that a generated manifest fell in the editable set under the original wording. Definition correction only: no new individual, no vocabulary change. Lessons remain 116, Best Practices 59."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.20.0 (MINOR) — BP-D26 enriched with the failure mode it prevents: a verification leaving no committed, re-runnable artifact proves the moment, not the property. MINOR rather than PATCH because this ADDS normative content adopters must follow, unlike the v2.19.1 amendment which corrected a defective clause. No new individual: 59 BP + 116 L unchanged."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.21.0 (MINOR) — L-85 enriched with freshness-against-origin: manifest self-verification is internal consistency and is silent on whether the snapshot is current. Adds normative content; 59 BP + 116 L unchanged."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.23.0 (MINOR) — added L-113, L-114, L-115 (per-item disposition on plural requests; classify findings at logging time; the cross-session handover inbox), correcting a real registration gap found by a cross-session finding (vaf-agentic-pipeline, 2026-09-09): OE_Operating_Discipline v2.4.0/v2.5.0 had cited these three rules under 'L-111'/'L-112'/'L-113', colliding with L-111 (documentation-coverage drift, v2.18.0) and L-112 (mechanical-repoint file-class discipline, v2.19.0) already registered under those IDs, and L-113 was never registered at all. Same shape as v1.32.0's own renumbering of a collision with v17.43.0's L-57 — verified against that precedent before choosing this remedy, not invented fresh. Lessons: 116 -> 119. Best Practices unchanged at 59. The discipline's citations are repointed in the same release (oe-pack v20.62.0); the v2.4.0/v2.5.0 historical notes are left as written, per this ABox's own L-114 (never correct a historical record by rewriting it)."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.24.0 (MINOR) — added L-116 (derivable versus stipulated decisions -- a stipulation ships as a proposal to the owner, not as an enforced artifact) and L-117 (a rule whose reach is decided by its author, not its adopters, is a retroactive-enforcement failure), from a real, independently-verified cross-session handover (a registrant package, 2026-09-10): between v1.242.0 and v1.253.0 that package added 18 SHACL shapes, 11 of them the session's own stipulations, and 7 of the last 8 lineage-discipline G-entries opened by citing an owner correction of one -- confirmed directly (G85-G92 exist, spot-checked entries genuinely cite an owner correction). New standing boundary B2b added to OE_Operating_Discipline citing L-116, between B1 and B2 as proposed. Lessons: 119 -> 121."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.25.0 (MINOR) — a real, published data corruption found and fixed while adding L-118: the v2.24.0 edit that inserted L-116/L-117 had silently dropped kb:Lesson_L_26_NoCommonAncestorBlocksDomainAssertion's own subject declaration, leaving its hasLessonId/label/dcterms:source/skos:definition attached directly to owl:NamedIndividual -- the OWL vocabulary term itself -- rather than to a proper individual. Live and unnoticed for one release cycle: the earlier edit's own verification checked total triple count and overall parse validity, never that the specific content near the insertion point remained correctly attached, which is the actual gap this closes. Restored from the last known-good published state, then verified comprehensively rather than by parse count alone: every hasLessonId and hasBestPracticeId subject checked to genuinely have 'Lesson' or a real BestPractice name in its local identifier, and owl:NamedIndividual confirmed to carry zero improper direct properties. Added L-118 (every governed element carries a human label, and discussion uses it) from the same handover that reported the label-before-identifier finding (a registrant package, 2026-09-10), verified directly: of 24 checked intent elements on that package's own register, exactly 12 carried neither rdfs:label nor hasTitle, matching the handover's own count precisely, though the specific shape name cited was not found under that name at verification time -- the underlying data claim held regardless. Lessons: 121 -> 122."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.26.0 (MINOR) — added L-119 (before creating a new fixture or deposit, check whether an existing one can be extended), from the owner's own direct observation: 27 fixture files had accumulated across oe-pack and oe-method with no consolidation step ever considered, one new directory per new gate. Applied in the same session, not left theoretical: oe-method's 3 separate per-gate negative fixtures (10 files) were consolidated into 1 combined fixture (6 files) that fails all three custom gates from one small tree, each gate re-run against the consolidated version and confirmed to genuinely still fail before the originals were removed. Lessons: 122 -> 123."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.27.0 (MINOR) — extended L-119, not rewritten: the owner's own direct observation that the fixture-file pattern was not new -- the same additive-only-growth shape had occurred before with patch files -- meant the lesson as first written, scoped by name to fixtures/deposits, risked not generalising to a future, differently-named recurrence. Extension added via a second dcterms:source value and an rdfs:comment (matching L-47's own precedent for extending a lesson without erasing what it originally said), plus a generalised paragraph appended to skos:definition. Added BP-D52 as the operational form: before creating a new file or directory for a specific need, name the closest existing artifact and check it for extension first. The prior fixture-specific incident this lesson was built from could not be independently re-located in the current tree at extension time -- disclosed rather than silently assumed resolved. Lessons: 123 (extended, not incremented). Best Practices: 60 -> 61."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.28.0 (PATCH) — extended BP-D52, not rewritten, in response to the owner's own follow-up: should the rule push harder toward reusing existing files? Checked first rather than strengthened by default -- no counter-lesson against over-consolidation existed, but BP-D6 (file naming must represent the file's own content) already bounds how far reuse can go, and pushing further would put BP-D52 in tension with BP-D6 and BP-D7's one-lineage-per-artifact principle. Added a Distinctness test grounded in BP-D6 instead: a need is genuinely distinct when the closest existing file's own name would have to misdescribe or double up if the content were folded in. A real parse error was caught and fixed during this edit -- a multi-paragraph value written with single-quote string syntax instead of triple-quote, caught by re-parsing before claiming success, per B3/L-95, not assumed correct from the edit alone. Lessons: 123 (unchanged). Best Practices: 61 (extended, not incremented)."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.29.0 (MINOR) — added L-120 (registration maintenance as a real ceremony, mirroring L-115's own handover inbox, not a threshold buried in a gate), from a direct impact-analysis request that found both an algebraic framework and an integration blueprint's closed registrations badly stale relative to real, verified current state -- an algebraic framework moved from registered v1.4.0 to a live-fetched v2.20.0 (MAJOR bump) during this session's own investigation, with real architectural changes (files deleted, not just added) occurring twice mid-investigation; an integration blueprint's own dependency shape on an algebraic framework changed twice since its registration closed, with zero remaining references to the pinned dependency anywhere in current tooling. The owner's own proposed fix, built this session: 08-registration-maintenance/ (registry, check tool, log), tested both directions before the first real run was logged (a synthetic within-threshold case correctly reported OK, the real an algebraic framework case correctly reported FLAG). Lessons: 123 -> 124."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.30.0 (MINOR) — added L-121 (a pinned dependency generation silently caps what a consumer can express, and the cap gets defended as a design decision, not reported as a constraint), from a genuine, self-critical cross-session finding (an integration blueprint session, 2026-09-17): an integration blueprint gave three successive answers for why it imported only 6 of an algebraic framework's operators, the first two wrong, the real cause -- an engine pin matching an older 6-operator ontology generation, not a design decision -- found only on the owner's third challenge. Duplicate-screened by the filing session against L-103/L-105/L-87; the distinction from L-103 verified directly against L-103's own stored text before accepting the screen's own claim, not taken on the filing session's word. A wrong guessed IRI in the seeAlso reference (L-103's real individual name differs from what pattern-matching the naming convention would suggest) was caught and fixed before this release shipped. Lessons: 124 -> 125."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.31.0 (MINOR) — added L-122 (a gate built for one thing to check naturally becomes all-or-nothing; once legitimately concurrent units of work exist, the same global evaluation deadlocks every unrelated one on any single unresolved finding) and L-123 (a tool comparing current state to an older tagged baseline for a rename-on-change versioned file must resolve by stable stem, never by today's exact filename -- the failure is silent, not an error), both from a real, verified cross-session proposal (a registrant package session, 2026-09-23), delivered directly to this inbox per L-113. Both defects found and fixed in that package's own backlog_lineage_order_check v1.7.0 -> v1.8.0 (shipped at that package's own v1.298.0); verified directly before acceptance, not taken on the filing session's word -- backlog:CrossLineageRiskAdvisoryShape confirmed to genuinely exist and support concurrent lineages, the --baseline scoping and stem-glob fallback confirmed present in the real, current tool file, the self-proof fixtures confirmed present, the full narrative confirmed present in that package's own changelog. Duplicate-screened against the existing knowledge base before adopting either -- the one candidate match (BP-D13, per-bundle vs ecosystem SemVer) checked and confirmed unrelated. Lessons: 125 -> 127. Follow-up done, not left pending: searched oe-pack's, oe-method's, and repo-tooling's own scripts directly for the same defect-class pattern (a tagged-baseline comparison for a rename-on-change versioned file) -- one match (oe_publish's own git tag -a) is tag creation, not a baseline lookup, and is not the same defect. No instance of the reported pattern found in this ecosystem's own shared tooling."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.32.0 (MINOR) — added L-124 (with SHACL rules merged, a derived triple satisfies an exemption like an asserted one; an exemption must read only what no rule derives, and its proof must run the production path) and extended L-36 (severity grades the whole shape, so a shape bundling conditions of different nature must be split before grading), both from real, verified a registrant package findings delivered through the L-84 pipeline. L-124 reproduced by the OEE session in three configurations before adoption; L-36 extension verified against the cited commit, shapes and audit amendment; both duplicate-screened. Lessons: 127 -> 128."@en,
        "knowledge_base ABox v2.33.0 (MINOR) — added BP-D53 (the three-file canonical structure: at most one T-Box, one A-Box and one SHACL file per subject, one shared ontology IRI, no combined, extension or patch files; the shipped vocabulary cited it as BP-D18, which is a different rule) and L-125 (a cited rule must resolve in the governed store and its enforcement must ship with it), from the owner's question of 2026-10-05."@en,
        "oe ABOX v1.5.0 (version-aligned)"@en,
        "oe ABox v1.6.0 (version-aligned)"@en,
        "oe ABox v1.6.2 (MINOR) — extended Lesson L-47 skos:definition with the constraint-compatibility clause empirically derived from Sprint F1 2026-05-14. Original L-47 text preserved in full; the extension adds three operational mitigation paths (supply data, relax constraint, reconsider redirect) and records the 9-Score-individual case as the surfacing instance. Per BP-D14: priorVersion v1.6.1. Per BP-D7: MINOR (additive extension to existing lesson; not a new lesson; not a breaking change)."@en,
        "oe PATCH v1.6.1. Sprint F1 ghost-reference cleanup: 0 dangling class references redirected to canonical homes; 0 dangling subClassOf claims dropped per L-47 (cross-subject methodological-vs-subsumption discipline). Per BP-D4/D5 gates: HermiT PASS, SHACL no new violations."@en,
        "ontology-engineering ABox v1.11.0 (MINOR) — added 3 meta-discipline Lessons (L-48, L-49, L-50) grounded in empirical drift analysis across 8 session transcripts (2026-05-10 through 2026-05-15). L-48: findings during execution do not authorize reopening closed decisions. L-49: options presented as co-equal must actually be co-equal per the catalogue. L-50: interrogative inflation — each clarifying question raises drift risk. Per L-47v2: each Lesson declared with mandatory skos:definition + dcterms:source."@en,
        "ontology-engineering ABox v1.12.0 (MINOR) — added L-51: Policy decisions have forward-going corollaries that bind subsequent decisions. Empirically grounded in 2026-05-15 drift episode where the AI shipped a one-off-scope bundle moments after the user established the family/derivative-only policy."@en,
        "ontology-engineering ABox v1.13.0 (MINOR) — adds BP-D21 (umbrella-vs-specific metric placement convention) and Lesson L-52 (narrow-interpretation-without-disclosure drift). Both grounded in empirical 2026-05-15 review episodes. Lesson count: 44 → 45. Best Practice count: incremented."@en,
        "ontology-engineering v1.14.0 (MINOR) per v17.23.0 L' — added L-46 (rdflib prefix rebinding masks raw IRIs) and BP-D22 (preserve prefixes on serialization). Lessons 45→46. BPs 21→22. Additive content only."@en,
        "ontology_engineering abox v1.10.0 (version-aligned)"@en,
        "ontology_engineering abox v1.8.0 (version-aligned to TBox)"@en,
        "ontology_engineering abox v1.9.0 (version-aligned to TBox)"@en,
        "ontology_engineering_abox v1.16.1 (PATCH) per v17.28.0 industrial-hardening — added CC BY 4.0 license, copyright, publisher/rightsHolder (IKÜ Computer Engineering), PROV-O wasGeneratedBy + wasAttributedTo (the method author). Additive ontology metadata only — no semantic changes."@en,
        "ontology_engineering_abox v1.7.0 (version-aligned to TBox; no content changes)"@en,
        "v2.34.0 (2026-10-06): adds BP-D54 (one T-Box, one A-Box and one SHACL file per package; modules; one archive triad), a changeNote on BP-D53 recording that its unit was superseded, and L-126 (a destructive override must name what it removes)."@en,
        "v2.35.0 (2026-10-06): a changeNote on BP-D54 recording the owner's ruling that a course repository is one package and its ontologies are counted per package, never per chapter."@en,
        "v2.36.0 (2026-10-06, MINOR): every named subject now carries dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> (its module), the first step of the consolidation of this package's files into one file per role. No term, label or definition changed. Also adds: a changeNote on BP-D54 recording how a module is marked (dcterms:isPartOf, not rdfs:isDefinedBy) and L-127 (a closed shape must be told about a new predicate before the predicate is added)."@en,
        "v2.37.0 (2026-10-06, MINOR): adds L-128 (a rule that skips what looks like X skips real subjects), L-129 (a gate that reads one file at a time changes its answer on the union), L-130 (an exemption named by an exact file name goes stale at each version), L-131 (an isolated interpreter ignores the variable that keeps it from writing bytecode) and L-132 (a release commit must not touch a workflow file), all from the consolidation of the packages into one T-Box, one A-Box and one SHACL file."@en,
        "v2.38.0 (2026-10-06, MINOR): adds L-133 (a measure that reads one value of a multi-valued property reads an arbitrary one) and L-134 (a text substitution of a prefixed name can hit the subject and rename a term), and corrects L-132, whose first recorded cause for the two untagged releases was wrong; the measured cause -- a tag ref whose workflow files differ from the repository's current ones, on four exhausted routes -- replaces it, with the correction recorded on the lesson."@en,
        "v2.39.0 (2026-10-06, MINOR): adds L-135 (filing into another package's inbox must not write a file that package's manifest covers) and L-136 (two modules declaring one term leave two definitions in one graph, and the term's namespace names which one governs)."@en,
        "v2.40.0 (2026-10-07, MINOR): adds L-137 (a debt line whose package is not in the scan was not measured, and reporting it CLEARED deletes another package's debt) and L-138 (the same repository measures under two package names, and a shared register can only carry the one its publisher stages), both from a finding another session filed with its own measurements."@en,
        "v2.41.0 (2026-10-07, MINOR): adds L-139 (a shared record that only one party may edit makes the rule it enforces impossible for everyone else to obey) and L-140 (a version token belongs to the file name, not to the content that moved into the file), and records the owner's ruling of 2026-10-07 as a change note on BP-D54: a package carries its own structure-debt register, and the governance package keeps the rules and a generated aggregate."@en,
        "v2.42.0 (2026-10-07, MINOR): records the owner's ruling of 2026-10-07 on examples as a second change note on BP-D54: examples are outside the domain ontologies' coverage and may hold their own T-Box, A-Box and SHACL file as a unit of their own. adds L-141 (before a file is renamed or repurposed, find every reader of its old name, including the readers that only report)."@en,
        "v2.43.0 (2026-10-07, MINOR): adds L-142 (an action taken once, at the event, with no later pass over what it missed, turns one refusal into a permanent gap)."@en,
        "v2.44.0 (2026-10-07, MINOR): records the owner's ruling of 2026-10-07 on registrations as a third change note on BP-D54: registrations obey the same three-file rule, each registrant a module of one registration unit. The classes of file and the questions that decide them are in OE_STRUCTURE_EXCEPTION_TAXONOMY_v1_0_0.md."@en,
        "v2.45.0 (2026-10-07, MINOR): adds L-143 (a union of two files does not drop the copies of an anonymous node, so a merge keeps both and a proof of no loss cannot see it)."@en,
        "v2.46.0 (2026-10-07, MINOR): adds L-144 (tools that each keep their own list of what not to read drift apart, and a skip decided by words in names removes real files without a word)."@en,
        "v2.47.0 (2026-10-07, MINOR): adds L-145 (a serializer can rewrite a literal's written form, so a proof of no loss must compare values and count the rewrites)."@en,
        "v2.48.0 (2026-10-07, MINOR): adds BP-D55 (one short release path that keeps every check) and L-146 to L-149 (a refusal that comes twice unchanged, a step done by hand twice, the cost of a late refusal, a wait recorded without looking); adds the later structure rulings as a change note on BP-D54. Best practices 63 -> 64, lessons 149 -> 153."@en,
        "v2.49.0 (2026-10-07, MINOR): adds L-150 (a check that takes minutes runs once per set of bytes) and extends BP-D55 with run-length rule R9, the publisher's gate receipt and the gate cache tool. Best practices 64, lessons 153 -> 154."@en,
        "v2.50.0 (2026-10-11, MINOR): amends BP-D47: four confidence tiers (D human judgment added), exactly one tier on every measurement:Score, the open place of TIER-D in the propagation order, the detection and mitigation now name the pack's SHACL shape in place of a utility and a CI test that exist in no OE repository, and the cross-LLM clause's evidence grades are no longer called TIER-A to TIER-C."@en,
        "v2.51.0 (2026-10-12, MINOR): BP-D47 records the owner's ruling of 2026-10-12 on the place of TIER-D: aggregations propagate the lowest tier in the order A, B, D, C."@en,
        "v2.52.0 (2026-10-12, MINOR): adds L-151 (a rule that exists only in prose is broken before it is enforced; the preventive action, the publisher name guard, is in force) and L-152 (a derived file that CI demands equal to its regeneration turns every legitimate shrink red; the preventive action is not yet adopted). Cases examined and not recorded as lessons are listed in the plan."@en,
        "v2.53.0 (2026-10-12, MINOR): L-152 records its preventive action as adopted (the debt aggregate check fails on growth and warns on a shrink; repo-tooling 1.48.0). No lesson added."@en,
        "v2.54.0 (2026-10-12, MINOR): adds L-153 (a delivery target that git cannot hold, an empty folder, does not exist for the sender); the preventive action, the inbox layout check, is in force (repo-tooling 1.49.0)."@en,
        "v2.55.0 (2026-10-12, MINOR): L-153 records its second preventive action, the manifest gate that warns when only the append-only handover log differs (repo-tooling 1.53.0). No lesson added."@en,
        "v2.56.0 (2026-10-19, MINOR): adds BP-D56 (every named class of an ontology file is linked to another class of its file, and the classes of a file form one connected model), on the owner's ruling of 2026-10-19. The check is oe_connectedness (repo-tooling), run by the publisher and by CI Gate C; the existing files are held by a baseline that may only fall. Best practices 64 -> 65."@en,
        "v2.57.0 (2026-10-19, MINOR): adds BP-D57 (the relationships the files use or state but do not link are discovered in three families, syntactic, semantic and temporal, with a trust level per candidate, and set, declared or rejected with a reason by a ceremony), on the owner's request of 2026-10-19. The check is oe_link_discovery (repo-tooling), run by the publisher and by CI Gate E; the existing sets are held by a baseline that may only fall. Best practices 65 -> 66."@en,
        "v2.72.0 (2026-10-22, MINOR): one kind rule on the owner's ruling of 2026-10-22 that Role is a real role (a function an agent holds, not a classification of agents): the range end of a characterisation link may be a role, as the link that gives an agent its role has a role at its range (DOLCE; Basic Formal Ontology: a role inheres in an independent continuant)."@en,
        "v2.71.0 (2026-10-21, MINOR): two class kinds on the owner's ruling of 2026-10-21: behavioural pattern (a recurring way an agent or system behaves, an occurrent; for the pathologies and drift categories of an agent) and method (an information artifact that says how a goal is achieved step by step, independent of where it sits in a lifecycle; Software and Systems Process Engineering Metamodel 2.0, method content). A failure type and a business impact are value domains and a failure mode is a quality; umbrella classes that group things of mixed kinds have no kind (a kind on them would contradict their children)."@en,
        "v2.70.0 (2026-10-21, MINOR): the kind rules reviewed against the sources, on the owner's request of 2026-10-21 to resolve the 33 links that did not fit: the rules of participation and of membership hold when either end of the link has the kind (the relations of Smith et al. 2005 run from the process to the continuant, and has member runs from the collection), the causal rule admits continuants as the Relations Ontology does, the provenance rule admits conceptual entities as PROV-DM does, attribution may end in a value domain (ISO/IEC 11179), and the category of measurement and assessment has its kind rule (23 kind rules, 2 further sources). The end named either is a new value of kb:atEnd."@en,
        "v2.69.0 (2026-10-21, MINOR): the taxonomy of relationships gains the category of measurement and assessment (33 categories), grounded in the Data Quality Vocabulary and the Semantic Sensor Network Ontology of the W3C, on the owner's ruling of 2026-10-21."@en,
        "v2.68.0 (2026-10-21, MINOR): BP-D61 and BP-D60 restated for the result: the 12 terms kept apart, the failure type and the 4 performance pairs merged on the owner's ruling, the homonyms given labels that name their sense, the detector's measure of the method vocabulary (no duplicate); the research record is v1.8.0."@en,
        "v2.67.0 (2026-10-21, MINOR): BP-D61 states the duplicate detector (rule S6, limits restated) and BP-D57 names the fourth family; no rule of BP-D61 changed."@en,
        "v2.66.0 (2026-10-21, MINOR): best practice BP-D61 added (one meaning, one term: a duplicate is merged and the other names become labels, on the owner's ruling of 2026-10-21); BP-D60 restated (its rule L3 now sends equal things to the merge, and its identifier no longer says that synonyms are linked); the synonymy category restated; the research record is v1.7.0."@en,
        "v2.65.0 (2026-10-20, MINOR): BP-D60 and the homonymy example corrected: reading every remaining pair of same-label terms of the method vocabulary found 6 homonyms and 1 polysemy, where the text had said none was found; the research record is v1.6.0."@en,
        "v2.64.0 (2026-10-20, MINOR): best practice BP-D60 (a name means one thing and a thing has one preferred name) added; the four lexical categories (synonymy, near-synonymy, homonymy, polysemy) added under lexical variant, grounded in 8 further sources opened and read; the research record is v1.5.0."@en,
        "v2.63.0 (2026-10-20, MINOR): BP-D59 limits updated: kinds recorded on 48 classes and categories on 26 properties of the method vocabulary (a ledger records the evidence for each; the head noun alone was refused for drift, failure mode and testing). No kind or rule changed."@en,
        "v2.62.0 (2026-10-20, MINOR): BP-D59 extended after a third research round (law, data standards, mathematics, software engineering) and a test on the method's own 1103 classes, on the owner's approval of the plan of 2026-10-20: kinds for the legal person, norm and legal document, master data, data element, value domain and data type, the mathematical object, the project, decision-making and decision, testing (case, suite, plan), the metric and measurement, the defect, error, failure and drift; six more kind rules (versioning, membership, direct sequence, cause and effect, the bearer of an extensive quality, the attribute a metric measures); 84 kinds, 14 facets, 20 rules, 36 further sources in all."@en,
        "v2.61.0 (2026-10-20, MINOR): BP-D59 extended after a second research round, on the owner's request of 2026-10-20 (physics, chemistry, biology, medicine, the humanities and philosophy): kinds for the organism, the body structure (cell, tissue, organ), the population and ecosystem, the specimen, the elementary particle, the pure substance (element, compound), the mixture, the spatial and temporal region, and the extensive and intensive quality; four new facets (stratum of reality, natural or nominal kind, level of biological organisation, extensive or intensive); the mobility facet dropped because sessility is a state of an individual and not a kind; 62 kinds, 14 facets, 24 further sources in all."@en,
        "v2.60.0 (2026-10-20, MINOR): adds BP-D59 (every class has a kind in the taxonomy of class kinds, and a relationship fits the kinds of its two ends), on the owner's request of 2026-10-20 to do the same research and taxonomy for classes, jointly with the taxonomy of relationships: 45 class kinds, 11 class facets with 27 values, 14 kind rules joined to the relationship categories, 12 more literature sources opened and read on 2026-10-20, and a ninth construction step (the kind of each end) in BP-D58. Best practices 67 -> 68."@en,
        "v2.59.0 (2026-10-20, MINOR): adds BP-D58 (a relationship is constructed from a need and a category of the taxonomy, not improvised) and the taxonomy it rests on, on the owner's request of 2026-10-20: 28 relationship categories (the four groups syntactic, structural, semantic and temporal, and five groups the literature keeps apart), 2 planes, 7 facets, 33 literature sources opened and read on 2026-10-20, and the 8 construction steps linked in sequence. Best practices 66 -> 67."@en,
        "v2.58.0 (2026-10-19, PATCH): the references that the texts of entries make to other entries by identifier (233) are rdfs:seeAlso links, set by the ceremony of BP-D57 on the first run of the check over the knowledge base. No entry added or removed, no text changed."@en ;
