    kb:hasSourceKind "secondary" ;
    kb:verifiedOn "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    skos:definition "What it gave to the taxonomy: Sessility is a lack of self-locomotion, a property of certain animals; sponges, corals, barnacles and oysters are sessile as adults, and sessile animals typically have a motile phase (sponge larvae). It is a property that changes in a life cycle, not a classification of organisms."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

