    rdfs:label "Survey-based naming conventions for use in OBO Foundry ontology development"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's request of 2026-10-20 (the same research and taxonomy for classes, jointly with the taxonomy of relationships) and the literature research of that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    dcterms:title "Survey-based naming conventions for use in OBO Foundry ontology development"@en ;
    dcterms:creator "Schober D. and others (BMC Bioinformatics)" ;
    dcterms:issued "2009" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2684543> ;
    kb:hasSourceKind "primary" ;
    kb:verifiedOn "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    skos:definition "What it gave to the taxonomy: Each concept has one editor-preferred name; alternative names (abbreviations, acronyms, translations) are exact synonyms stored in the ontology; a name must mean the same thing every time, so homonyms are avoided in preferred names."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

kb:RelationshipCategory_Synonymy a kb:RelationshipCategory,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Synonymy"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's request of 2026-10-20 (synonyms, homonyms and the lexical concerns of the taxonomies) and the literature research of that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    skos:broader kb:RelationshipCategory_LexicalVariant ;
    kb:belongsToPlane kb:RelationshipPlane_Representation ;
    kb:groundedInSource kb:LiteratureSource_SynonymWiki,
        kb:LiteratureSource_SKOSRef,
        kb:LiteratureSource_TermSynonymy,
        kb:LiteratureSource_OBONaming,
        kb:LiteratureSource_WordNet ;
    kb:exemplifiedBy skos:altLabel,
        skos:exactMatch ;
    skos:definition "Two terms carry the same meaning in the same sense (sodium chloride and NaCl). Synonymy is tested by substitution in a given sense, absolute synonyms are rare, and a claim of synonymy names the sense. Within one thing a synonym is an alternative label; two things of one vocabulary with the same meaning are one thing and are merged (BP-D61); an exact match, which is symmetric and transitive, is kept only for equal things that must live in different vocabularies."@en ;
    skos:example "the reliability and the testing copies of the regression test: one definition in two classes, merged into the testing class with the other name kept as a label."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

kb:RelationshipCategory_NearSynonymy a kb:RelationshipCategory,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Near-synonymy"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's request of 2026-10-20 (synonyms, homonyms and the lexical concerns of the taxonomies) and the literature research of that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    skos:broader kb:RelationshipCategory_LexicalVariant ;
    kb:belongsToPlane kb:RelationshipPlane_Representation ;
    kb:groundedInSource kb:LiteratureSource_SynonymWiki,
        kb:LiteratureSource_SKOSRef ;
    kb:exemplifiedBy skos:closeMatch ;
    skos:definition "Two terms overlap in a semantic field without being interchangeable in every sense or register. The things they name are linked by a close match, which is symmetric and not transitive, so that errors do not compound along a chain."@en ;
    skos:example "A term and a term that can replace each other in some contexts and not in others."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

kb:RelationshipCategory_Homonymy a kb:RelationshipCategory,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Homonymy"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's request of 2026-10-20 (synonyms, homonyms and the lexical concerns of the taxonomies) and the literature research of that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    skos:broader kb:RelationshipCategory_LexicalVariant ;
    kb:belongsToPlane kb:RelationshipPlane_Representation ;
    kb:groundedInSource kb:LiteratureSource_PolysemyWiki,
        kb:LiteratureSource_OntoLex,
        kb:LiteratureSource_OBONaming,
        kb:LiteratureSource_WSD ;
    skos:definition "Two unrelated things share one form by coincidence (bear, the animal, and bear, the verb). Lexicographers give them separate entries and ontology-lexicon models give them separate lexical entries. In an ontology the preferred labels of two different classes, or of two different properties, must differ, so that a name means one thing; a class and a property may share a label because their kind tells them apart."@en ;
    skos:example "The animal bear and the verb bear in a general lexicon. In the method's own vocabulary: Class richness names both the instances per class and the share of classes that have instances, and Consistency score names both a measure of an ontology and a measure of the outputs of a language model."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

kb:RelationshipCategory_Polysemy a kb:RelationshipCategory,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Polysemy"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's request of 2026-10-20 (synonyms, homonyms and the lexical concerns of the taxonomies) and the literature research of that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    skos:broader kb:RelationshipCategory_LexicalVariant ;
    kb:belongsToPlane kb:RelationshipPlane_Representation ;
    kb:groundedInSource kb:LiteratureSource_PolysemyWiki,
        kb:LiteratureSource_OntoLex,
        kb:LiteratureSource_WSD ;
    skos:definition "One form has several related senses (get: to procure, to become, to understand). Ontology-lexicon models give one lexical entry several senses, each referring to its own ontology element. How finely the senses are divided depends on the application: coarse distinctions are easy to agree on and fine ones are not."@en ;
    skos:example "A term used for an activity and for its result, told apart by two classes with sense-specific labels."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

