    kb:appliesToCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Characterization ;
    kb:atEnd "range" ;
    kb:requiresKind kb:ClassKind_Quality ;
    kb:groundedInSource kb:LiteratureSource_SoftwareMetric ;
    skos:definition "A metric is applied to an attribute, the property of a system or process that is measured, and a measurement is the number it gives; the end that is measured is a quality."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-20T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

kb:KindRule_CausalContinuants a kb:KindRule,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Cause and effect may be continuants"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's request of 2026-10-21 (complete the remaining work on kinds and categories by the recommended method; review the 33 links that did not fit) and the literature read on that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    kb:appliesToCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Causal ;
    kb:atEnd "both" ;
    kb:requiresKind kb:ClassKind_Continuant ;
    kb:groundedInSource kb:LiteratureSource_RO,
        kb:LiteratureSource_Avizienis2004,
        kb:LiteratureSource_QualityInteraction ;
    skos:definition "The Relations Ontology has causal relations between processes (causal relation between processes) and also between continuants (causal relation between entities; causally influences) and between a material entity and a process; a dormant fault is a state that causes an error; one quality characteristic affects another. So a cause or an effect is a continuant or an occurrent, and an abstract thing (a proposition, a concept) is neither."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-21T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

kb:KindRule_CharacteristicValueDomain a kb:KindRule,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "A characteristic takes its value from a value domain"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's request of 2026-10-21 (complete the remaining work on kinds and categories by the recommended method; review the 33 links that did not fit) and the literature read on that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    kb:appliesToCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Characterization ;
    kb:atEnd "range" ;
    kb:requiresKind kb:ClassKind_ValueDomain ;
    kb:groundedInSource kb:LiteratureSource_ISO11179,
        kb:LiteratureSource_DOLCE ;
    skos:definition "A thing has a level, tier, class or rank when a characteristic of it takes a value from a set of permitted values: the value domain of the metadata registry model, which DOLCE calls a region of a quality space. The end that holds the permitted values is a value domain, so attribution has either a quality or a value domain at its range."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-21T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

kb:KindRule_CharacterizationRole a kb:KindRule,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "A role can be the characteristic that a thing takes"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's ruling of 2026-10-22 (Role is a real role: a function an agent holds, not a classification of agents) and the literature read on that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    kb:appliesToCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Characterization ;
    kb:atEnd "range" ;
    kb:requiresKind kb:ClassKind_Role ;
    kb:groundedInSource kb:LiteratureSource_DOLCE,
        kb:LiteratureSource_BFOGround ;
    skos:definition "A characterisation link joins a bearer to what characterises it, and a role is one such thing: DOLCE has a role as a concept that a thing plays, and the Basic Formal Ontology has a role inhere in a bearer without being part of its nature. So the link that gives an agent its role has a role at its range, as well as a quality or a value of a value domain."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-22T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

kb:KindRule_CharacterizationBearer a kb:KindRule,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "An agent or a process can bear a characteristic"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's request of 2026-10-21 (complete the remaining work on kinds and categories by the recommended method; review the 33 links that did not fit) and the literature read on that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    kb:appliesToCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Characterization ;
    kb:atEnd "domain" ;
    kb:requiresKind kb:ClassKind_Agent,
        kb:ClassKind_Occurrent ;
    kb:groundedInSource kb:LiteratureSource_DOLCE,
        kb:LiteratureSource_BFOGround ;
    skos:definition "A role is played by an agent, and a process has qualities of its own: DOLCE has qualities of perdurants (events and processes) beside qualities of endurants, and a role is played by an endurant; the Basic Formal Ontology has a role inhere in an independent continuant. So the bearer end of an attribution may be an agent or an occurrent, as well as a material entity, an information artifact or a quality."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-21T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

kb:KindRule_AssessmentEvaluator a kb:KindRule,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "An assessment link has an evaluator at one end"@en ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's request of 2026-10-21 (complete the remaining work on kinds and categories by the recommended method; review the 33 links that did not fit) and the literature read on that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    kb:appliesToCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Assessment ;
    kb:atEnd "either" ;
    kb:requiresKind kb:ClassKind_Metric,
        kb:ClassKind_Measurement,
        kb:ClassKind_Process,
        kb:ClassKind_Agent,
        kb:ClassKind_Device,
        kb:ClassKind_TestCase,
        kb:ClassKind_TestSuite,
        kb:ClassKind_Method ;
    kb:groundedInSource kb:LiteratureSource_DQV,
        kb:LiteratureSource_SOSA,
        kb:LiteratureSource_SoftwareMetric,
        kb:LiteratureSource_SoftwareTesting ;
    skos:definition "One end of a link that measures, evaluates, detects or verifies is what evaluates: a metric (a standard to measure a quality dimension, DQV), a measurement (the evaluation of a resource against a metric, DQV), an observation or a test, which is an act (SOSA: the act of carrying out a procedure), or a sensor, which is a device, an agent or software (SOSA). The other end is what is evaluated or found: a quality dimension, any resource, the property of a feature of interest, a result, a pathology. The sources fix the evaluator and state no kind for the evaluated end (DQV: any resource; SOSA: any feature of interest), so the rule constrains the evaluator only; that gap is stated and not filled. A method is also an evaluator end (the Semantic Sensor Network Ontology has an observation use a procedure). A test case and a test suite are also evaluators: the software testing sources define a test as the check of a result against a case, so the test case or the test suite is the evaluating end of a link to its result."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-21T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo oe-prov:Agent_MethodAuthor .

kb:BestPractice_D59_EveryClassHasAKindAndARelationshipFitsTheKindsOfItsEnds a kb:BestPractice,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "BP-D59: Every class has a kind in the taxonomy of class kinds, and a relationship fits the kinds of its two ends; the kind rules of the relationship categories say which pairs are allowed"@en ;
    kb:hasBestPracticeId "BP-D59"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    dcterms:source "The owner's request of 2026-10-20 (the same research and taxonomy for classes, jointly with the taxonomy of relationships) and the literature research of that date, recorded in RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/knowledge-base> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso kb:BestPractice_D58_ARelationshipIsConstructedFromANeedAndACategoryNotImprovised,
        kb:BestPractice_D56_EveryClassIsLinkedAndTheClassesOfAFileFormOneModel,
        kb:BestPractice_D57_MissingLinksAreDiscoveredDecidedAndSetNeverLeftAsText,
        kb:ConstructionStep_Kinds,
        kb:RelationshipCategory_TemporalOrder,
        kb:ClassFacetValue_Dependence_GenericallyDependent ;
